--TEST--
Text outside the tags is copied to the output byte for byte: `<?` alone and `#!` past offset 0 are text, `<?=` echoes, and `<?php` inside a string is data (`rule:statements/nvs-is-the-only-open-tag`, `rule:tooling/shebang-opens-code-mode`)
--FILE--
Report <? draft #! not a shebang <?= "v2" ?> end
<?nvs
// covers: tools:cli/files-extensions-and-tags
// Only `<?nvs` opens code. Inside code, the tags below are the content of a string.
echo "<?php is data here", "\n";
?>
footer
<?nvs echo "done", "\n";
--EXPECT--
Report <? draft #! not a shebang v2 end
<?php is data here
footer
done
